{
  // Emits the `.d.ts` tree the converter reads — and nothing else.
  //
  // Two things depend on it, and both fail silently without it. The converter's component
  // roster is the intersection of the storybook titles and the package's *exported* names, and
  // that export list comes from a declaration file: with none, all 14 titles drop as
  // `[TITLE_UNMAPPED]` and the build writes zero components. The second is the payload — each
  // emitted `<Name>.d.ts` is the API contract the design agent codes against, extracted from
  // these declarations. `RibbonProps`, `SyncProgressProps`, `TableColumn<Row>` and
  // `CardImageProps` are real interfaces in `packages/ui/`; without an emit they would be guesses.
  //
  // Separate from the app's own programs because those are `noEmit` and always will be — this
  // is an app, and `pnpm build` type-checks rather than emits. Extending the base they extend
  // (`tsconfig.base.json`) keeps the `paths`, `strict` and `jsx` settings identical, so the
  // declarations describe the same code the app compiles.
  "extends": "../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": false,
    "declaration": true,
    "emitDeclarationOnly": true,
    // `allowImportingTsExtensions` is legal under `emitDeclarationOnly`, but nothing in `packages/ui/`
    // uses it and leaving it on would let one in unnoticed.
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": false,
    // Errors do not block the emit (`noEmitOnError` defaults false) — deliberately. This is a
    // *view* of the source for a documentation tool; a type error in `packages/ui/` is `pnpm verify`'s
    // to fail, not this file's, and half a declaration tree is worth more than none.
    "rootDir": "..",
    "declarationDir": "./dist",
    "declarationMap": false,
    "composite": false,
    "incremental": false
  },
  // `entry.ts` is the barrel; `../packages/ui` is everything it re-exports. `preview-runtime.tsx` is
  // deliberately absent — it is the preview harness, not API, and a declaration for it would
  // put the fake backend into the surface the design agent reads.
  "include": ["../packages/ui", "./entry.ts"],
  // Tests and stories are not API. They emit harmlessly, but they land in the same tree the
  // converter globs and every one of them is a file ts-morph then has to parse.
  //
  // **And the three files the app's own program leaves out, which this list has to repeat**: an
  // `exclude` written here replaces the one `extends` would have brought; it does not add to it.
  // The web host's two Workers and its service worker are compiled under the `WebWorker` lib, by
  // programs of their own (`packages/ui/tsconfig.web-worker.json`, `tsconfig.web-sw.json`). Under
  // this program's `DOM` they were seven of the nine errors this build printed on 2026-10-08 —
  // `DedicatedWorkerGlobalScope` is not a name here — and an error is not harmless to the build
  // even though it does not stop the emit: `tsc` exits non-zero, and `buildCmd` chains the
  // reference build after it with `&&`. Nothing imports the three (the page names each by URL),
  // so leaving them out takes nothing from the barrel. A fourth file the root `tsconfig.json`
  // excludes owes a line here.
  "exclude": [
    "../packages/ui/**/*.test.ts",
    "../packages/ui/**/*.test.tsx",
    "../packages/ui/**/*.stories.tsx",
    "../packages/ui/lib/core/web/worker.ts",
    "../packages/ui/lib/core/web/scanWorker.ts",
    "../packages/ui/lib/core/web/sw/sw.ts"
  ],
  "references": []
}
